/-!
# The three-rank of the concrete Tits group

Two explicit words in the certified Parrott generators generate a nonabelian
subgroup of order 27. Their commutator is central and has order three.
Three successive cyclic extensions collect every element into one of 27
words; their images of point zero are distinct. The certified ambient order
makes this subgroup Sylow. Every abelian subgroup of a nonabelian group of
prime-cube order is proper, giving three-rank at most two.

The balanced permutation tables cache the two longer words. Their comparison
with the original generator words, orders and commutation identities are all
checked by kernel reduction; the discovery calculation supplies no assumptions.
This proof does not classify two-locals or assume even characteristic.

Source: Parrott, *A Characterization of the Tits' Simple Group* (1972), §5,
p.683, using the conventions in
`refs/original/n-group-global/parrott-tits-presentation.md`; the rank bound is
used in Aschbacher–Smith, Theorem 0.1.2(1), printed pp.3–4 and 481–482.
-/

